<title>FRANCE: Rouen August flour exports fell to 52,979 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Rouen August flour exports fell to 52,979 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flour exports from the French port of Rouen fell to 52,979 tonnes in August 1996 from 69,000 tonnes in August 1995, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Flour destinations break down as follows (in tonnes)</p>
<p>    Estonia...2,461    West Africa..............7,155</p>
<p>    Sudan....20,419    Algeria..................3,000</p>
<p>Yemen....19,944</p>
<p>In Rouen one ship was currently loading 9,500 tonnes of flour destined for Angola.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
